is halloween ends really the end and why  does its star think the film will make  fans very angry here's all you need to  know before the big premiere  the official release date for halloween  ends is october 14th 2022 just in time  for the holiday filming for halloween  ends initially began in january 2022 and  concluded a few months later in march  pre-pandemic blumhouse studios had  planned to release halloween kills in  october 2020 and halloween ends one year  later in 2021 of course delays due to  kova 19 through a wrench into production  so the pair of sequels were pushed back  by ear studios generally like to release  halloween films well around halloween  which seems like a no-brainer you know  it's halloween i guess everyone's  entitled one good scare  this was the case for the first five  original halloween films which all  debuted theatrically in the month of  october the sixth just barely squeaked  in with a september 29th release date  this trend was surprisingly dropped in  favor of summer releases for halloween  h2o and halloween resurrection as well  as rob zombie's duo of reboots however  with the appearance of david gordon  green's new trilogy halloween has  returned to its classic fall schedule  with halloween ends wrapping up the  tradition by releasing around the same  time of year as its predecessors  the 2018 halloween film brought jamie  lee curtis back to the iconic role of  lori strode and introduced two new  generations in lori's daughter karen  played by judy greer and her  granddaughter allison played by andy  matacik though this central trio  survived that film and made it to the  climax of the follow-up halloween kills  ended on a shocking note as michael  murdered karen just before the credits  started so many people are dead we're  not equipped curtis and matacik are back  one last time in halloween ends with  james jude courtney and original actor  nick castle joining forces to bring  michael myers to life as they did on the  two previous entries kyle richards is  also back once again as lindsay wallace  laurie's 1978 babysitting charge who  managed to again narrowly escape  michael's knife in halloween kills  trilogy mainstays will patton and omar  dorsey round out the returning cast  members joining the cast is former  guiding light star michael o'leary as dr  mathis a character mentioned but not  seen in halloween kills rowan campbell  of hulu's the hearty boys will also  provide a fresh face as a new character  named corey cunningham  the official synopsis for halloween ends  explains that rather than picking up  exactly where we left off in halloween  kills the story will resume four years  later lori strode and her granddaughter  allison are living together and there's  no michael myers in sight we can assume  that the movie will have lori and  michael locked in a final showdown of  sorts at least a final showdown for this  iteration of the franchise as for the  fate of these two characters who can say  for certain in an interview with total  film magazine jamie lee curtis producer  malaika cod and director david gordon  green gave a few hints as to what  audiences might expect from the final  film in the trilogy after halloween  kills focused on the town of haddonfield  at large it seems like we're in for a  shift with a cod revealing that the  final film in the trilogy will be in his  words way more contained  it's disgusting  as for green he went on to elaborate  slightly suggesting that the final  halloween film which was originally  planned to take place on the same 2018  halloween night as both its predecessors  may be something fans won't expect he  told total film i get engaged by doing  something different if i was just going  to be repetitive i would hand the reins  off to someone else when you have that  opportunity within an established  franchise it's really fun to think about  how you can show different tones and  perspectives and evolve  the iconic not so sleepy town of  haddonfield illinois is one of the most  infamous movie towns in horror history  and also one of the deadliest while the  original john carpenter film was shot in  los angeles county the most recent  halloween trilogy traveled to the  opposite coast to film the 2018  halloween was mostly filmed in the low  country of south carolina the second  installment halloween kills was filmed  mostly in north carolina interestingly  halloween ends was shot primarily in and  around the savannah georgia area though  not exclusively according to the film's  imdb page photography for ends also took  place in part around salt lake city utah  a vast departure from the east coast  locations and the film's midwestern  setting leaving fans wondering just  where the final installment might take  us  the new halloween trilogy beginning with  the 2018 film is largely the brainchild  of filmmakers and long time  collaborators david gordon green and  danny mcbride though green and mcbride  were both new to the horror genre they  were long time fans of john carpenter  and deborah hill's original 1978  halloween and opted to ignore all the  previous sequels and remakes green went  on to direct all three films in this new  trilogy evidently even though they  ignored all the previous installments in  the franchise it still reportedly took  green and mcbride more than 80 drafts of  the screenplay to get it right with  rewrites happening as late as one week  before production according to the  hollywood reporter michael myers loose  with a bunch of nut bags and hadn't  failed on halloween night the duo of  green and mcbride returned to write the  screenplay for halloween kills alongside  scott teams resulting in a sequel that  proved more polarizing than its  crowd-pleasing predecessor green and  mcbride also co-wrote the screenplay for  halloween ends this time alongside paul  brad logan and chris bernier  when 2018's halloween was released it  was a simpler time the film arrived in  theaters and then quickly made its way  to home video soon after with the second  and third films in david gordon green's  planned trilogy being greenlit almost  immediately following its success  unfortunately it would be another three  years before halloween kills would be  released due to the coven 19 pandemic  with the sequel's initial release of  october 2020 being shifted to october  2021 halloween ends began filming not  long after the release of halloween  kills with a set release date for  october 2022 with only a year between  these two films green's two sequels will  follow an 80 slasher movie tradition of  immediate back-to-back entries the  earlier halloween series even  sporadically followed this pattern for a  while halloween 2 was released in  october 1981 continuing the story from  the first film with the largely  unrelated halloween 3 season of the  witch coming out a year later  in october 1988 halloween four the  return of michael myers was released  which brought myers back from his  comatose state leading into halloween  five the revenge of michael myers the  following october halloween ends is set  to arrive in theaters on october 14th  2022 and as with halloween kills before  it will also be made available on  peacock for the first 60 days of the  film's release the halloween franchise  is a bit complicated but most  long-running horror series are including  halloween ends there are 13 total films  in the saga though not all of them are  necessary to enjoy this final trilogy  installment the only movie in the  anthology that every film tends to stem  from is the original 1978 halloween  which introduced the world to both  michael myers and laurie strode this  masterpiece has become an icon over the  past four decades and no matter how many  new halloween sequels or reboots hit the  screen none can escape the shadow of the  original the original halloween 2  halloween 4 the return of michael myers  halloween 5 the revenge of michael myers  and halloween 