ebooted trilogy of slashers she  told enemy it's going to make people  very angry and it's going to be shocking  because it asks a lot of questions so  that's all i can tell you wherever the  conclusion to this modern halloween  trilogy takes us it seems it will be  somewhere we've never gone before this  might be scary to some longtime michael  myers fans but the possibility of an  unprecedented and surprising conclusion  may be just the kind of uncertainty the  halloween franchise needs  for more than 40 years jamie lee curtis  has come and gone from her role as the  iconic final girl lori strode  continuously escaping the clutches of  michael myers now halloween ends  promises well an end to all that evil  dies tonight this means that either lori  is set to die in combat against michael  or live happily ever after once he's six  feet under whichever ending befalls our  horror heroine it will surely be  thrilling to see her story get a  definitive conclusion here jamie lee  curtis has implied in a video promoting  halloween ends that this is her last  time playing lori strode she went on to  explain to total film i'm not saying  something like oh because i die it's  nothing to do with that i'm talking  about emotionally what they've  constructed i think it will be a  spectacular way to end this trilogy  with a title like halloween ends there  are some pretty serious implications  attached no doubt this is the end to  david gordon green's sequel trilogy of  halloween films meant to be a love  letter of sorts to the original john  carpenter classic with jamie lee curtis  evidently satisfied with the film's  conclusion and the plot seemingly  wrapped up here it sounds like halloween  ends might actually be the final chapter  of the halloween saga and what better  film to end on than the 13th of course  john carpenter has his own thoughts on  the continuation of the halloween brand  carpenter told comicbook.com if you take  a dollar sign and attach it to anything  it 